--
N5008 [temp.mem]/1, [dcl.fct]/3: the out-of-line definition of a member
function template of a non-template class names its parameters differently
from the in-class declaration (`__f, __l' vs `first, last'); the body refers
to the definition's names.  The definition's parameter list must be grafted
together with its body.  Previously the body kept the declaration's names, so
the instantiated body failed with "symbol '__f' is unknown" (libstdc++'s
std::filesystem::path::_S_convert).  The `if constexpr' chain and the
deduced return type are the header's shape.
